The original is already minimal. This version only drops the `operator[]` call: it computes the address directly from `fields.data()`. It does the same bounds check, so it returns the same pointer or `FIT_NULL` for every input. Any speedup will be small, and it may disappear entirely once the compiler inlines the original.

```cpp
FieldDefinition* MesgDefinition::GetFieldByIndex(const FIT_UINT16 index)
{
    const size_t count = fields.size();
    if (static_cast<size_t>(index) < count)
        return fields.data() + index;

    return FIT_NULL;
}
```